Rule 1 (output tensor, if provided, must have the same shape as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 3 (when input is floating or complex, output tensor keeps the same dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (if dtype_(v_1) = 6 then dtype_(v_2) = 6) ∧ (if dtype_(v_1) = 7 then dtype_(v_2) = 7) ∧ (if dtype_(v_1) = 8 then dtype_(v_2) = 8) ∧ (if dtype_(v_1) = 9 then dtype_(v_2) = 9) ∧ (if dtype_(v_1) = 10 then dtype_(v_2) = 10)
>>
Rule 4 (when input is integer, output tensor must be float32 or float64)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5) then (dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8)
>>
Rule 5 (input tensor should not be bool or string dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11
